    "rationale": "The raw score is a weak tier signal: held-out precision per 0.1 score band peaks at 0.57 and falls again at the top bands, so no score cut-off reaches the strong target (score_table_validation). The lead (the card's score minus the best other condition's score) does separate (lead_table_validation), so tiers are bands of lead. Targets (share of cards in the tier that are the simulated condition): strong >= 80%, moderate >= 40%, weak >= 25%. Each cut-off is the lowest lead that reaches its target plus 3 points on the calibration run (twice the size of the held-out run), so the held-out numbers are not tuned. Cut-offs: strong lead >= 0.1, moderate lead >= 0.03, weak lead >= 0.01; a lower lead is not shown. No card below score 0.2 or with fewer than 3 specific terms. Held-out precision: strong 0.82, moderate 0.44, weak 0.28. Every tier has a cut-off that meets its target, so the strength word stays in the patient UI.",
